**Definition 6.4 (counted replay and memory selection from raw).** `RunN`
starts at the same encoded irreducible entrance and copies $1^n$ to a
countdown. Until empty, execute precisely one Step of Definition 5.1,
feeding its next typed consumed bit from Definition 6.3; optionally emit
Definition 5.3's patch and update the constructor/role maps, then tail
the countdown. An absent required bit or illegal represented row fails.
This is one literal row per iteration, including older converter rows.

To select memory from raw $W$, first perform only the basic scans of
Definition 6.3, run `RunN`, require its full physical endpoint equals $W$,
then perform Definition 6.2 using that derived history. For an M-body first
parse its seven lists and do basic extraction directly; replay precedes
reselection and exact M-body comparison. This order avoids a circular
premise in partial-object role classification.

